<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:controls="using:Midora.Avalonia.Controls"
        x:Class="Midora.Avalonia.Windows.TimelineGenerationHelpDialog"
        x:CompileBindings="False"
        Title="Batch Create Help"
        Width="880" Height="740" MinWidth="690" MinHeight="460"
        Background="{DynamicResource Brush.Surface.0}"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        CanResize="True"
        ExtendClientAreaToDecorationsHint="True"
        ExtendClientAreaChromeHints="NoChrome">
  <Border BorderBrush="{DynamicResource Brush.Border.Strong}" BorderThickness="1">
    <Grid RowDefinitions="36,*,58">

      <!-- Custom title bar (WPF WindowChrome substitute). Escape is handled by the IsCancel Close button. -->
      <Grid Grid.Row="0" Background="{DynamicResource Brush.Black}">
        <Border Background="Transparent" PointerPressed="OnTitleBarPointerPressed" />
        <TextBlock x:Name="TitleText" Margin="11,0,44,0" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   FontWeight="SemiBold" IsHitTestVisible="False" Text="Batch Create Help" />
        <Button Classes="caption close" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Click="OnCloseClick"
                ToolTip.Tip="Close">
          <controls:FluentIcon Classes="captionicon"
                               Foreground="{DynamicResource Brush.Text.Secondary}"
                               Data="{StaticResource WindowControl.Close}" />
        </Button>
      </Grid>

      <!-- Scrolling help content. -->
      <ScrollViewer Grid.Row="1" Padding="18,15"
                    HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                    VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto">
        <StackPanel>

          <Border Margin="0,0,0,13" Padding="16"
                  Background="{DynamicResource Brush.Surface.1}"
                  BorderBrush="{DynamicResource Brush.Border}"
                  BorderThickness="1" CornerRadius="5">
            <StackPanel>
              <TextBlock Classes="section" Margin="0,0,0,8"
                         Text="1. Start with a small candidate count" />
              <TextBlock Classes="muted" TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="19"
                         Text="Base Tick is an origin in the current editor's time coordinates. Tick expressions return offsets from that origin, not absolute Project ticks. The current editing cursor supplies the default Base Tick. Start with 16 or 128 candidates, inspect the result, then increase the count." />
              <TextBlock Margin="0,8,0,0" Classes="muted" TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="19"
                         Text="Every non-empty expression starts with =; for example =96 or =t0 + 96. A blank field reuses its previous value. Initial fields accept ordinary finite numbers, not expressions. Blank Initial fields use the displayed defaults. Math functions such as Sin, Max, Clamp and Round work without a Math. prefix. Ctrl+Space opens completion." />
            </StackPanel>
          </Border>

          <Border Margin="0,0,0,13" Padding="16"
                  Background="{DynamicResource Brush.Surface.1}"
                  BorderBrush="{DynamicResource Brush.Border}"
                  BorderThickness="1" CornerRadius="5">
            <StackPanel>
              <TextBlock Classes="section" Margin="0,0,0,8" Text="2. Understand an iteration" />
              <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Variables}">
                <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                  <DataTemplate>
                    <Grid Margin="0,0,0,8" ColumnDefinitions="150,*">
                      <TextBlock Classes="mono" Foreground="#DCDCAA" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                 Text="{Binding Label}" />
                      <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Classes="muted" TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="19"
                                 Text="{Binding Text}" />
                    </Grid>
                  </DataTemplate>
                </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
              </ItemsControl>
              <TextBlock Classes="muted" TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="19"
                         Text="All expressions are evaluated from the same previous state. Current-result dependencies are ordered automatically, not by the order of the fields in the dialog. For example, Gate =g0 + 1 and Velocity =g1 * 2 are valid. Circular dependencies (Gate =v1 and Velocity =g1) and referencing a field's own result are rejected. After all fields have been computed, the whole result is normalized and becomes the next previous state." />
              <TextBlock Margin="0,8,0,0" Classes="muted" TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="19"
                         Text="Create first object from initial values is OFF by default: candidate i=0 runs all expressions using normalized Initial values as *0. When ON, candidate i=0 uses Initial values directly and counts toward Maximum Candidates; expressions first run at i=1. The checkbox is saved in presets." />
            </StackPanel>
          </Border>

          <Border Margin="0,0,0,13" Padding="16"
                  Background="{DynamicResource Brush.Surface.1}"
                  BorderBrush="{DynamicResource Brush.Border}"
                  BorderThickness="1" CornerRadius="5">
            <StackPanel>
              <TextBlock Classes="section" Margin="0,0,0,8"
                         Text="3. Stopping, rounding and collisions" />
              <TextBlock Classes="muted" TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="19"
                         Text="Maximum Candidates counts attempted candidates, including objects later removed by collisions. It defaults to 65,535 and cannot exceed 16,777,216. An enabled Maximum Relative Start Tick is inclusive: the first rounded start beyond it stops generation, even if later iterations might return to the range. It limits the start, not the end of a note." />
              <TextBlock Margin="0,8,0,0" Classes="muted" TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="19"
                         Text="Integer fields use midpoint rounding away from zero. Negative relative Tick becomes 0. Note Velocity is clamped to 1–127, Key to 0–127, and Gate to at least 1 and at most the remaining representable Tick range. Event values follow the active lane's range and type (including Boolean/Enum normalization). Initial values are normalized too; iteration inputs are not unbounded raw values. Absolute Tick overflow, non-finite results, invalid dependencies, target validation failures or an exhausted resource budget fail the entire operation." />
              <TextBlock Margin="0,8,0,0" Classes="muted" TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="19"
                         Text="Notes: at the same start Tick and Key, existing notes win; between generated candidates, the earlier iteration wins. Events: at the same Tick and lane target, the last candidate wins and replaces all existing points at that exact key. Other imported duplicates remain untouched. A constant Tick can therefore retain only one object; it still consumes all requested candidates." />
              <TextBlock Margin="0,8,0,0" Classes="muted" TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="19"
                         Text="Generation is prepared in bounded pages off the UI thread, then published as one Undo operation. Cancel or any failure publishes nothing. Working buffers and resident staging each have a 64 MiB limit; owned spill has a 16 GiB limit, and the overall result-record budget also applies. A candidate count is not a promise that disk or result capacity is sufficient. Validate checks settings, syntax and dependencies; only generation can check every iteration's runtime result and final collisions." />
            </StackPanel>
          </Border>

          <!-- 4. Examples. -->
          <TextBlock Classes="section" Margin="0,0,0,8"
                     Text="4. Practical examples — simple patterns to note art" />
          <TextBlock Margin="0,0,0,12" Classes="muted" TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="19"
                     Text="Examples use Tick units, not beats. Unlisted expressions are blank (identity), and the Initial checkbox is OFF unless stated. Change the Tick spacing to suit your project's resolution. No example changes the Base Tick." />
          <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Examples}">
            <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
              <DataTemplate>
                <Border Margin="0,0,0,12" Padding="16"
                        Background="{DynamicResource Brush.Surface.1}"
                        BorderBrush="{DynamicResource Brush.Border}"
                        BorderThickness="1" CornerRadius="5">
                  <StackPanel>
                    <TextBlock Classes="section" Margin="0,0,0,8" Text="{Binding Title}" />
                    <TextBlock Margin="0,0,0,10" Classes="muted" TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="19"
                               Text="{Binding Description}" />
                    <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Fields}">
                      <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                        <DataTemplate>
                          <Grid Margin="0,0,0,6" ColumnDefinitions="170,*">
                            <Border Margin="0,0,12,0" Padding="8,5"
                                    BorderBrush="{DynamicResource Brush.Border}"
                                    BorderThickness="1" CornerRadius="3">
                              <TextBlock VerticalAlignment="Center" Text="{Binding Label}" />
                            </Border>
                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" VerticalAlignment="Center" Classes="mono"
                                       Foreground="#DCDCAA" TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="{Binding Text}" />
                          </Grid>
                        </DataTemplate>
                      </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                    </ItemsControl>
                  </StackPanel>
                </Border>
              </DataTemplate>
            </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
          </ItemsControl>

          <Border Padding="16"
                  Background="{DynamicResource Brush.Surface.1}"
                  BorderBrush="{DynamicResource Brush.Border}"
                  BorderThickness="1" CornerRadius="5">
            <StackPanel>
              <TextBlock Classes="section" Margin="0,0,0,8" Text="5. Reuse safely" />
              <TextBlock Classes="muted" TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="19"
                         Text="Note and Event generation have independent preset lists under Data/Presets. Presets store expressions, Initial values, the initial-object checkbox, candidate count and optional relative limit. They never store Base Tick, the current owner or the lane target. Applying an Event preset to a different lane uses that lane's type and range. Presets are revalidated for their tool, expression profile, numeric contract, syntax and resource limits. Duplicate preset names are rejected instead of overwriting another preset." />
              <TextBlock Margin="0,8,0,0" Classes="muted" TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="19"
                         Text="CC10/71–78 use the editor range -64..63: Initial values, p0, p1 and recurrence feedback all stay in this range; results are translated to MIDI only when creating points. Example: displayed 32 with =p0*0.5 becomes displayed 16 (MIDI 80). Project Mapping still operates on MIDI values: value*0.5 maps MIDI 96 to 48 (display -16). Other CC and Logical Parameters keep their own ranges." />
              <TextBlock Margin="0,8,0,0" Classes="muted" TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="19"
                         Text="Expressions are bounded pure numeric expressions, not C# scripts: no loops, assignments, object creation, files, processes or arbitrary APIs. Each expression body is limited to 8,192 Unicode scalars, 512 syntax nodes and 64 levels of nesting. Generation settings and expression code are not stored in the Project; only the resulting ordinary notes or events are." />
            </StackPanel>
          </Border>
        </StackPanel>
      </ScrollViewer>

      <!-- Footer. -->
      <Border Grid.Row="2" Padding="12,10"
              Background="{DynamicResource Brush.Surface.1}"
              BorderBrush="{DynamicResource Brush.Border}"
              BorderThickness="0,1,0,0">
        <Button HorizontalAlignment="Right" Classes="primary" Width="112"
                IsDefault="True" IsCancel="True" Content="Close" Click="OnCloseClick" />
      </Border>
    </Grid>
  </Border>
</Window>
